     <article class="story single" data-beat="education">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">EDUCATION</span> · Education (aggregate) · 2026-11-07 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>CM Vijay's Govt Accuses DMK of AI-Generated Low-Quality Books</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#AI</span> <span>#Scam</span> <span>#DMK</span> <span>#CM Vijay</span></div>
       <p>CM Vijay's Government has leveled an accusation against the DMK, alleging the use of Artificial Intelligence (AI) to generate low-quality books. This claim, highlighted by NDTV Profit, raises questions about the integrity of published materials.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-07/cm-vijays-govt-accuses-dmk-of-ai-generated-low-quality-books.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The accusation positions this event as potentially &quot;India's First AI Scam,&quot; drawing attention to the emerging challenges and ethical considerations surrounding the deployment of artificial intelligence in public services and education.</p><p>Further details regarding the specific books and the alleged AI involvement are anticipated.</p><p>What to watch: Developments in the investigation and responses from the DMK.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The draft accurately reports the claims made in the source headline and summary without overstepping into unverified territory.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://news.google.?oc=5" rel="noopener">Education (aggregate)</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
