     <article class="story single" data-beat="national">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · The Hindu · 2026-11-07 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Congress leader K.C. Venugopal predicts resignation of Chief Election Commissioner</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>AICC general secretary K.C. Venugopal has stated that Chief Election Commissioner Gyanesh Kumar will soon be forced to resign. Speaking at a rally in Kozhikode, Venugopal accused Prime Minister Narendra Modi and Home Minister Amit Shah of leveraging the Election Commission to undermine the Congress party and manipulate electoral outcomes in Haryana, Maharashtra, and Karnataka.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-07/congress-leader-kc-venugopal-predicts-resignation-of-chief-e.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Venugopal further alleged that 13.32 crore voters have been improperly deleted from electoral rolls. He criticized the 2023 amendment to election commissioner appointment laws, claiming it grants excessive legal immunity and removes the Chief Justice of India from the selection process, contrary to previous Supreme Court judgments.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Accurately captures the specific allegations made by K.C. Venugopal as described in the source text.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/kerala/gyanesh-kumar-will-soon-be-forced-to-step-down-says-kc-venugopal/article71678914.ece" rel="noopener">The Hindu</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
