       <h1>Defence Minister Rajnath Singh to Celebrate Diwali with Troops at Border</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Defence</span> <span>#India</span> <span>#Diwali</span> <span>#Rajnath Singh</span></div>
       <p>Defence Minister Rajnath Singh is scheduled to celebrate Diwali with soldiers at the Nathu La frontier, according to DD India. This initiative marks the Minister's engagement with military personnel during the festive period.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-07/defence-minister-rajnath-singh-to-celebrate-diwali-with-troo.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>News Arena India reports that Minister Singh will also meet Indian Army personnel at Bagdogra on Diwali Eve. This suggests a multi-location visit as part of his festive observance with the armed forces.</p><p>The Defence Minister's Diwali celebrations with the Indian Army will encompass both West Bengal and Sikkim, as detailed by News18. Combining these reports, Minister Singh's engagements include meetings with troops at Bagdogra on Diwali Eve, followed by Diwali day celebrations at the Nathu La frontier, spanning key military locations in the eastern region.</p><p>What to watch: Further details on the Defence Minister's frontier visits.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: A well-synthesized report that effectively aggregates information from multiple provided outlets to provide a comprehensive view of the Minister's itinerary.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMitwFBVV95cUxOLURjemQzMmpXZmhMN0ZRWWlMTGZpQnZGa212aHk3djVSVjA1RHU4bWMtY1FfTE0xNFdXc3hHRzRsSVU3X3FWU2NyTEJuWlFfYnlRVV9CQTJja2U2UzQ5a0V3T0JGYnl6SGZHN2RoWWk1eHlTLTRhOWdvbDBvUEVuVmdhVDVKVEVCRi1hcEMtYnVOSm9ULXRYZGJJTWJCc0w0UkdBVGRrNnViS2paSDczZDFtX1NUMzA?oc=5&amp;hl=en-US&amp;gl=US&amp;ceid=US:en" rel="noopener">Defence (aggregate)</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
