     <article class="story single" data-beat="sports">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">SPORTS</span> · NDTV Sports · 2026-11-07 · editor 9/10 · 2 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Hardik Pandya Traded to Punjab Kings for Arshdeep Singh</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#IPL</span> <span>#Cricket</span> <span>#Player Trade</span> <span>#Hardik Pandya</span></div>
       <p>Star all-rounder Hardik Pandya is set to move to Punjab Kings in exchange for pacer Arshdeep Singh, following an agreement between Mumbai Indians and Punjab Kings ahead of the upcoming IPL auction. This proposed trade marks Hardik's return to a new franchise after his second tenure with Mumbai Indians, while Arshdeep will join the five-time IPL champions. The deal awaits ratification from the BCCI for official confirmation. An IPL source confirmed the completion of the trade, noting that Hardik is content to play under Shreyas Iyer, who will continue as captain for Punjab Kings.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-07/hardik-pandya-traded-to-punjab-kings-for-arshdeep-singh.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>According to the IPL source, the decision to trade Hardik for Arshdeep was made by the captain and coach. Arshdeep has had a long association with Punjab Kings, developing significantly with the franchise. While acknowledging the difficulty for owners to part with Arshdeep due to his strong performances, the leadership ultimately proceeded with the decision. This move concludes Hardik's second stint with Mumbai Indians, where he had returned in the 2024 season as captain, replacing Rohit Sharma.</p><p>Hardik's captaincy with Mumbai Indians did not yield the desired results, as the team failed to qualify for the play-offs in two of the three seasons under his leadership. Similarly, parting with Arshdeep, who has become India's leading wicket-taker in the shortest format and broken into the international setup through his IPL performances, was a significant decision for Punjab Kings. Shreyas Iyer has led Punjab Kings to their first IPL final since 2014 last year, and Hardik will join the team strictly as a player, focusing on his all-round abilities.</p><p>The trade aligns with the BCCI's extension of the player retention deadline to November 17, allowing sufficient time for formalities before the mini-auction in Goa on December 16. Punjab Kings also contemplate releasing Marcus Stoinis and Nehal Wadhera prior to the auction. Hardik, however, has not played competitive cricket since the previous IPL season due to multiple injury setbacks, a factor Punjab Kings will consider as they hope to strengthen their all-round department.</p><p>What to watch: BCCI's ratification of the trade ahead of the December 16 mini-auction.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Thorough reporting of the reported Hardik Pandya trade for Arshdeep Singh, incorporating all major background details.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://sports.ndtv.com/cricket/hardik-pandya-traded-to-punjab-kings-arshdeep-singh-moves-to-mumbai-indians-report-12297209#publisher=newsstand" rel="noopener">NDTV Sports</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
