       <h1>India-Australia Defence Ties Deepen Amid China's Assertiveness</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Defence</span> <span>#Geopolitics</span> <span>#Asia-Pacific</span></div>
       <p>Defence ties between India and Australia are reportedly gaining &quot;strategic depth,&quot; according to The Shillong Times. This strengthening of bilateral relations is occurring amidst an environment of &quot;China's assertiveness&quot; in the region.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-07/india-australia-defence-ties-deepen-amid-chinas-assertivenes.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The enhanced cooperation between the two nations signifies a growing alignment in their strategic interests. While specific initiatives or agreements were not detailed, the term &quot;strategic depth&quot; implies a substantial increase in the scope and intensity of their defence engagement.</p><p>This development is framed directly in response to China's regional posture, suggesting a coordinated effort to address evolving geopolitical challenges. The report highlights the increasing importance of such alliances in maintaining regional stability.</p><p>What to watch: Future joint defence initiatives between India and Australia.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The draft is a concise and accurate summary of the provided source snippet.</p>
