       <h1>Manchester City Leads WSL Title Race Ahead of Chelsea Clash</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#sports</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Manchester City moved two points clear at the top of the Women's Super League following a 5-0 victory over West Ham. Khadija Shaw scored a hat-trick in the win, bringing her season tally to 12 goals in nine appearances.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-07/manchester-city-leads-wsl-title-race-ahead-of-chelsea-clash.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Meanwhile, Chelsea was held to a 1-1 draw by Everton at Stamford Bridge, resulting in a loss of their top-of-the-table position. The two clubs are scheduled to face each other next week in a potential title-deciding match. Chelsea played without the injured Lauren James, while City's dominant performance successfully narrowed the goal difference gap between the league leaders.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief is accurate and well-structured, capturing the significant shift in the WSL standings and the upcoming fixture.</p>
