       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">TECH</span> · Engadget · 2026-11-07 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Modders Port Game Boy Titles to Tamagotchi Paradise</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#tech</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>The 2025 Tamagotchi Paradise device has gained a new following due to its unexpected moddability. Reddit users have successfully ported and played Game Boy Color titles, including Pokémon Gold and Silver, on the handheld hardware. One modder demonstrated that the devices can even facilitate Pokémon trading by connecting two modified units.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-07/modders-port-game-boy-titles-to-tamagotchi-paradise.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Another user successfully ran the original Tamagotchi Game Boy title on a White Glacier model. While the device was met with mixed reviews at launch, these modifications offer a novel way for enthusiasts to utilize the hardware for retro gaming, transforming the digital pet device into a makeshift portable console.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief effectively summarizes the Engadget report on Tamagotchi modding while maintaining brevity.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.engadget.com/2310126/people-are-modding-the-tamagotchi-paradise-to-run-game-boy-games/" rel="noopener">Engadget</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
