       <h1>Six Killed in Krakow Market Square Shooting</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#world</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>A gunman in military attire opened fire at random in Krakow’s Main Market Square on November 7, 2026, killing six people and injuring at least 15 others. Police engaged the suspect in a gunfight, ultimately wounding and arresting him. Two police officers are among the injured, with one in critical condition.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-07/six-killed-in-krakow-market-square-shooting.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Authorities recovered multiple weapons and ammunition from the attacker's vehicle. While the suspect is a Polish citizen, no motive has been confirmed for the attack in the historic city center. Officials have cordoned off the area as investigations continue, urging residents and tourists to avoid the square.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief accurately summarizes the core facts of the source material without padding or unverified claims.</p>
