     <article class="story single" data-beat="national">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · News18 India · 2026-11-07 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Tamil Nadu Probes Periyar Library Book Procurement Irregularities</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>The Tamil Nadu government is investigating book purchases for Coimbatore’s Periyar Arivulagam library following allegations of inflated prices, factual errors, and suspected AI-generated content. Writer Perumal Murugan, a committee member, flagged instances such as a classic text misidentified as a &quot;poet and philosopher&quot; and claims that books were sourced from specific publishers at prices exceeding ₹1,400.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-07/tamil-nadu-probes-periyar-library-book-procurement-irregular.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>School Education Minister A Rajmohan confirmed an inquiry into procurement records from the previous government's tenure. Political controversy has intensified, with accusations of corruption regarding the library's management. Officials are currently reviewing files to determine if substandard or fraudulent books were procured.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Concise and accurate; covers all key allegations and the official investigation status without fluff.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.news18.com/india/poet-and-philosopher-error-suspected-ai-content-tamil-nadu-probes-periyar-library-book-purchases-ws-l-10416570.html" rel="noopener">News18 India</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
