     <article class="story single" data-beat="tech">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">TECH</span> · Engadget · 2026-11-07 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>TSA guidelines for traveling with video game consoles</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#tech</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Travelers may bring game consoles through TSA checkpoints, though specific packing requirements depend on battery type and equipment size. Devices with lithium-ion batteries, such as handheld systems and most controllers, must be kept in carry-on luggage to mitigate fire risks associated with thermal runaway. If asked, travelers may need to power on these devices to verify their function.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-07/tsa-guidelines-for-traveling-with-video-game-consoles.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>While home consoles like the PlayStation 5 are permitted in checked baggage, experts advise keeping them in carry-on bags to prevent damage from harsh handling. This also reduces the risk of property loss, which accounted for approximately 63.5 percent of TSA consumer claims between 2002 and 2025.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief effectively synthesizes the TSA guidelines and safety advice while maintaining a professional, concise tone.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.engadget.com/2305767/gamers-tsa-game-console-rules/" rel="noopener">Engadget</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
